Scenario-based — Answer commands only

Discard local changes (not staged): git restore filename

Remove file from staging (keep changes): git reset <file>

Fix wrong commit message (not pushed): git commit --amend -m "Corrected commit message"

View commit history readable: git log --oneline

Set name & email globally after cloning:
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "youremail@example.com"

View unstaged edits: git diff

Switch to feature/login: git checkout feature/login (or) git switch feature/login

Recover deleted branch (not pushed):
git reflog
git checkout -b feature-ui <commit_hash>

Upload local commits to remote: git push origin main (or appropriate branch)

Fetch without merging: git fetch origin

Create & switch to search-filter: git checkout -b search-filter (or) git switch -c search-filter

Remove committed API key from history: use filter-branch command (see above)

See all local & remote branches: git branch -a

Merge feature/signup into main:
git checkout main
git merge feature/signup

Resolve merge conflict in app.js (commands):
# edit app.js to resolve markers
git add app.js
git commit

Stop tracking .log and node_modules/:
echo "*.log" >> .gitignore
echo "node_modules/" >> .gitignore
git rm -r --cached node_modules/
git add .gitignore
git commit -m "Update .gitignore"

Who changed line 25 in script.py: git blame -L 25,25 script.py (or) git blame script.py

Save work to switch branches quickly: git stash

Restore stashed changes: git stash apply (or) git stash pop

Delete feature/test locally: git branch -d feature/test

Safely delete feature-ui after merge: git branch -d feature-ui

Delete unmerged branch feature-experiment (force): git branch -D feature-experiment

Deleting feature-ui while on feature-login: ensure you are not on feature-ui, then run git branch -d feature-ui

Before deleting bugfix-footer check merged status: git branch --merged

Delete multiple merged branches at once: git branch -d feature-a feature-b feature-c

Remote-work commands (short answers)

Clone remote repo: git clone https://github.com/username/repository.git

See remotes: git remote -v

Add new remote: git remote add origin https://github.com/username/repository.git

Remove remote: git remote remove origin

Rename remote: git remote rename origin upstream

Fetch updates (no merge): git fetch origin

Pull and merge: git pull origin main

Push commits: git push origin main

Push first time & set upstream: git push --set-upstream origin feature-branch

Change remote URL: git remote set-url origin https://github.com/username/new-repository.git

List remote branches: git branch -r

Clean up deleted remote branches locally: git remote prune origin

Fetch specific branch: git fetch origin feature-branch

Show remote details: git remote show origin

Rebase local onto remote branch:
git fetch origin
git rebase origin/main
